00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.810
And that's pretty-- that
can be really detrimental.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.360
And so if you look at
it from a standpoint,

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.400
let's say we've got an API team.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.510
They're ready to release their
APIs or build their APIs.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.817
They start out happy.

00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:33.400
But they get to this
first standpoint,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.150
which is they have an
architecture review.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.780
So now that's a speed bump.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.660
Then they have to go
to API design review.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.202
Someone has to make
sure that they're

00:05:40.202 --> 00:05:42.900
using the right approach
and they're reusable,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.150
and making sure they have
the right policies in there.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.950
Or they have an internal
