00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:30.020
So if we take a look at
the security policies,

00:25:30.020 --> 00:25:32.900
you're going to be able to see,
well, there are multiple ones.

00:25:32.900 --> 00:25:36.110
And within the
platform, let's say

00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:38.600
if you're interested in
using a token-based mechanism

00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:41.600
to authenticate each and
every API call, of course

00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:46.250
within the platform, you can use
JWTs, JWT tokens, J-W-T tokens.

00:25:46.250 --> 00:25:49.290
You can use SAML
assertions, for example.

00:25:49.290 --> 00:25:50.780
You can use encrypted tokens.

00:25:50.780 --> 00:25:53.390
You can use basic
authentication.

00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:56.570
If you're looking forward to
enforce OAuth across the board,

00:25:56.570 --> 00:25:58.190
of course, you
can do it as well.

00:25:58.190 --> 00:26:01.040
OK, so there are multiple
options within the platform.

00:26:01.040 --> 00:26:03.050
And of course, there's
a lot of flexibility

00:26:03.050 --> 00:26:05.060
for you to choose and
enforce the right pattern

00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:06.740
depending on your business.

00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:07.550
OK?

00:26:07.550 --> 00:26:08.410
RAYMOND PENG: Nice.

00:26:08.410 --> 00:26:09.410
RUBEN GONZALEZ: Awesome.

00:26:09.410 --> 00:26:11.330
So again, there
are multiple ones.

00:26:11.330 --> 00:26:13.310
Remember, security
isn't all about just

00:26:13.310 --> 00:26:15.230
